{
  "_comment": [
    "Recipes for turning raw screenshots into publishable guide images.",
    "Boxes are [left, top, right, bottom] as fractions of the image, so they",
    "hold up if a screenshot is retaken at a different window size.",
    "The crop drops the left sidebar, which is where the profile photo,",
    "display name, username and Snapcode all live. Removing that region is",
    "better than painting over it: nothing identifying survives the crop.",
    "Cover boxes are measured off the cropped image, not estimated, so they",
    "sit inside the element and do not swallow its label."
  ],
